        "question": "In relation to food preservation, indicate with a tick whether each of the following statements is true or false: Micro-organisms are inactivated by freezing; Melons, pears and bananas freeze well; Food should be frozen quickly at -25°C.",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "Statement 1 — Micro-organisms are inactivated by freezing: TRUE. Freezing lowers the temperature to -18°C or below, which halts the growth and reproduction of micro-organisms, although it does not destroy them; they become dormant and can reactivate on thawing. Statement 2 — Melons, pears and bananas freeze well: FALSE. These fruits have a very high water content; when frozen, ice crystals form and rupture cell walls, causing a soft, mushy, unacceptable texture on thawing. Statement 3 — Food should be frozen quickly at -25°C: TRUE. Rapid freezing at -25°C forms small ice crystals that cause minimal damage to cell structure, preserving texture, nutritional value and appearance; slow freezing produces large crystals that damage food quality.",
