        "label": "2(a)(i)",
        "question": "Evaluate the design of the jacket shown in the diagram. Refer to: function (use); comfort when wearing; aesthetic appeal.",
        "marks": 12,
        "model": "Evaluation of the jacket design: Function (use): The jacket shown is a casual outerwear garment suitable for everyday wear in mild weather conditions. It appears to have a front zip/button fastening which protects the wearer from wind and light rain while allowing easy on/off; pockets provide practical storage for keys, phone and wallet. The collar or hood (if present) gives additional protection to the neck. The relaxed cut allows freedom of movement for walking and everyday activity. Comfort when wearing: The jacket's loose, unstructured cut allows easy layering over a t-shirt or light jumper; it does not restrict arm movement. If the fabric has stretch or a comfortable lining, the jacket can be worn for extended periods. Raglan or set-in sleeves both allow movement; a smooth lining allows the jacket to slide easily over clothing. Adjustable cuffs and a drawstring hem (if featured) allow the fit to be adapted for warmth. Aesthetic appeal: The jacket has a contemporary, casual aesthetic suited to teenage and young adult wearers; its clean lines and simple silhouette make it versatile and easy to combine with different outfits. Colour choice is important — a neutral colour (navy, grey, black) or a bold accent colour makes the jacket a versatile or statement piece respectively. Minimal branding and logo detail give a modern, understated look that appeals to a wide range of consumers.",
