        "question": "Describe the following types of food poisoning:\nInfectious Food Poisoning\nToxic Food Poisoning",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "Infectious food poisoning is caused by consuming food contaminated with harmful bacteria such as Salmonella or Campylobacter. The bacteria multiply in the digestive system, causing symptoms like vomiting, diarrhoea and fever. Toxic food poisoning occurs when food contains toxins (poisons) produced by bacteria such as Staphylococcus aureus. The toxin is pre-formed in the food before it is eaten; symptoms appear rapidly and include nausea and vomiting.",
