        "question": "Describe the following types of pensions:\nContributory old age pension\nNon-Contributory old age pension",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "Contributory Old Age Pension (State Pension Contributory): paid to people aged 66+ who have made sufficient PRSI (Pay Related Social Insurance) contributions during their working life. The amount received is based on the number of contributions paid; it is not means tested. Non-Contributory Old Age Pension (State Pension Non-Contributory): paid to people aged 66+ who do not qualify for the contributory pension or who have insufficient PRSI contributions. It is means tested, so income and assets are assessed to determine entitlement and rate.",
        "diagram": "",
        "model_source": "ai-h1"
